  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"terminal#15834\", \"terminal#16237\", \"terminal#19993\"], \"answer\": \"Windows Terminal already supports this, so no new feature is needed. Edit settings.json (Settings > Open JSON file) and set the profile's colorScheme to an object with separate light and dark entries, for example: \\\"colorScheme\\\": { \\\"light\\\": \\\"One Half Light\\\", \\\"dark\\\": \\\"One Half Dark\\\" }. Use \\\"Tango Light\\\" and \\\"Campbell\\\" (or any schemes you like) in place of those names. The profile then switches color scheme when the app theme changes. Set the Terminal's theme to \\\"Use Windows theme\\\" so it follows the system theme. This is not yet available in the Settings UI, which is tracked in #14475, so for now it has to be configured in the JSON file. The docs are under Profile appearance > Color scheme on learn.microsoft.com.\"}",
